This method is used to perform a right node rotation, which is a type of tree rotation where the left child of the node is moved up as the parent of the original node, and the original node is moved to the right child of the left child. This rotation helps to balance the tree is some cases.

The method takes a node as an input parameter, and it returns a new parent of the node as an output. The purpose of the method is to rotate the node to the right and update the tree structure accordingly.

The method first checks if the node is not null, if so, it will extract the left child of the node and assign it to a new variable. Then, it sets the right child of the node to the right child of the left child, and sets the left child of the node to the new parent. Finally, it returns the new parent.

If the node is null, the method will return a null value, indicating that there is no new parent.

It's important to note that this is a helper method for the tree balancing algorithm, and it is used to maintain the balance of the tree.

